an be corrupted mid-operation. (4) Not safe + not idempotent: append with wall-clock timestamp and possible mid-append crash \u2014 partial entries and divergent logs. For an append-only log with at-least-once delivery, quadrant (2) is the critical failure: it shows that safety without idempotency does not survive duplicate delivery. Therefore the log must require idempotency. Safety is a secondary concern that matters only if intermediate states are observable 
